Commercial S3.2 long-poll retry-classification diagnosis
=========================================================

Observed at: 2026-08-29T16:08:36Z
Service: tu1nz-adult-commercial-s3.service
Installed Application before correction:
1743d4bf94a3f722648e206827da640980394613

Safe symptom
------------

The service had reached startup phase 18 READY, produced GREEN health and
processed the terms acceptance plus synthetic creator verification. The next
Telegram long-poll transport failure terminated the process with exit status 2
and safe code S3_TELEGRAM_FAILURE_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED. The final health record was
RED for PROCESS and POLLING. Restart remained no and NRestarts remained zero.

At failure time the durable product state contained zero submissions, zero
payments and zero publications. A later image and the correctly selected JPEG
document arrived only after the process was already inactive, so neither was
processed by the Application.

Proven root cause
-----------------

The shared Telegram wire reports an expired long-poll transport as
TELEGRAM_TIMEOUT and a transient connection failure as TELEGRAM_NETWORK_ERROR.
The Commercial S3 adapter mapped both safe codes to the generic
S3_TELEGRAM_FAILURE. The supervisor treats that generic code as non-retryable,
so the first ordinary transport interruption exhausted the failure budget
immediately instead of using the already implemented bounded exponential retry.

The timestamps are consistent with this exact path: the final successfully
processed update and cursor save preceded the exit, and the exit followed one
long-poll network interval. No product handler, database mutation, media import,
payment or publisher error occurred.

Correction boundary
-------------------

Only TELEGRAM_TIMEOUT, TELEGRAM_NETWORK_ERROR and TELEGRAM_RATE_LIMITED are
normalized to the existing retryable TELEGRAM_API_UNAVAILABLE code. All other
unknown Telegram errors remain fail-closed as S3_TELEGRAM_FAILURE. Each failed
poll now emits only a safe code, retryable flag and bounded attempt count; no
token, request/response body, chat identity or media is logged.

Regression coverage drives the actual S3 Telegram client and runtime supervisor
through each transient code, proves one-second bounded retry, a successful
second poll and no restart. The full local Application suite passes 716/716.

